#====================================================================
# DRAFT-littlefs-stdio-guard-undef-ohos.kv
# littlefs 2.11.2 上游测试框架 #undef _STDIO_H 在 OHOS sysroot 触发 stdio.h 重入重定义
# Draft only. Do not promote into knowledge/graph until promoted.
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-littlefs-stdio-guard-undef-ohos
trigger_tool:           clang|make
phase:                  compilation|testing
error_signature:        redefinition of enumerator 'FDSAN_ERROR_LEVEL_FATAL'|
                         redefinition of '_G_fpos64_t'|typedef redefinition.*fpos_t|
                         stdio.h included multiple times|redefinition of 'fdsan_owner_type'
severity:               3
category:               toolchain|libc|testing|ohos
match_keywords:         _STDIO_H, _FEATURES_H, stdio.h, include guard, redefinition,
                         fpos_t, fdsan, test_runner, test framework, musl, OHOS, sysroot,
                         included multiple times, undef, header reentrancy, feature macros
title:                  Upstream test frameworks that #undef _STDIO_H/_FEATURES_H to allow
                         feature-macro re-inclusion break on OHOS/musl sysroot stdio.h
root_cause:             Some upstream test frameworks (e.g. littlefs runners/test_runner.h)
                         explicitly `#undef _FEATURES_H` and `#undef _STDIO_H` after an
                         initial `#include <stdio.h>`, relying on glibc-style per-type
                         header guards that make stdio.h safely re-includable. The OHOS
                         sysroot stdio.h (musl/OHOS style) defines fpos_t/_G_fpos64_t and
                         the fdsan enums inline without per-type guards, so a second
                         include after the undef redefines _G_fpos64_t/fdsan_error_level
                         and fails compilation.
rec_approach:           Pre-define the _STDIO_H guard via CFLAGS so the framework's first
                         stdio.h include is skipped and the post-#undef include becomes the
                         single processing site. Library build is unaffected — apply only
                         to the test-runner/generated-test compilation.
rec_command: |
  # littlefs example: build test-runner with the guard pre-defined
  CFLAGS="-fPIC -O2 -D_STDIO_H" make test-runner CC=<ohos-clang> AR=llvm-ar
  # do NOT put -D_STDIO_H into the library build; it only fixes the test framework
solution_cmds: |
  # Equivalent patch alternative (not required if CFLAGS guard is used):
  #   runners/test_runner.h: guard the two #undef lines so they are skipped on
  #   sysroots whose stdio.h is not safely re-includable.
verification: Run the upstream test suite end-to-end after the fix, e.g.
  `./scripts/test.py ./runners/test_runner -b -k` → 11606/11606 passed, 0 failed
  (littlefs 2.11.2, OHOS aarch64 clang 15, 28741 power-loss scenarios).
fallback:               Patch test_runner.h to skip `#undef _STDIO_H` under a compile-time
                         macro; keep `#undef _FEATURES_H` (features.h re-inclusion is safe).
doc_refs:               E119,E020,E493
applies_to:             any-C-library-whose-upstream-test-framework-undefs-stdio-guards,
                         littlefs
last_updated:           2026-09-07